WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.420
- Well, I see an upright bass behind you

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.705
and I'm just curious, I mean,

00:00:03.705 --> 00:00:04.980
can I convince you

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.740
to play just a little
something, maybe, or?

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.420
- Uh, yes, well you know,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.240
I don't know if I have any basses nearby,

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.202
but if I did...

00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:13.342
(clapping)

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:16.433
(both chuckling)

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:17.640
- Amazing!

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.200
- How about Blues in B flat?

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.350
- I love it!

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.017
(low strumming)

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:29.814
(tapping sound)

00:00:32.354 --> 00:00:34.863
- [Kelly] Something is
moving your camera around.

00:00:34.863 --> 00:00:35.696
It's awesome.

00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:37.491
- Oh, that was my tapping
foot, sorry, ha ha ha!

00:00:37.491 --> 00:00:38.632
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:38.632 --> 00:00:39.740
I tell you what.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:41.905
- It was like, tapping with
the beat, like moving...

00:00:41.905 --> 00:00:43.944
You play so well!

00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:46.880
Lester, at some point in life
when we can be within six feet

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.730
of each other, we gotta
do something together.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.440
I wanna sing while you play bass!

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.477
- That's what I'm talking
about, I would love that.

00:00:52.477 --> 00:00:56.160
You know, I always play my
basses, but I find it's like a...

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.320
It's become a ritual
now before my newscast,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.288
I put on some music in
my little home office

00:01:00.288 --> 00:01:02.810
and then I start jamming
and it kinda gets me in this

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.002
like, head space, to do
the news every night.

00:01:05.002 --> 00:01:06.114
Thanks for asking.

00:01:06.114 --> 00:01:06.947
(Lester chuckling)

00:01:06.947 --> 00:01:08.970
- Yeah, no I love it!

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.700
Kyle, like I was tellin' you before,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.910
my bass player is so amazing.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.990
He'll go like, how you have
your upright bass back there,

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.820
he'll go, you know, from
different kind of basses

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.376
and it's just such a smooth sound...

00:01:18.376 --> 00:01:19.353
- Oh, I love it!

00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:21.402
- Few people know this, but actually,

00:01:21.402 --> 00:01:22.820
they always think it's the drummer,

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.290
but it's the bass and the
drums that really hold down

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.820
the rhythm and everything of a set.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.110
- [Lester] Yeah if you could
out the bass track, ya know,

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.759
you would realize how much a part of...

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:34.610
You don't often hear it consciously,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.630
but man, you take it, you
remove it from the music

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:37.910
and everything changes.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.527
- Yeah, and then it's like,
"Wait, where's the, where's beat

00:01:40.527 --> 00:01:41.803
"and where's everything", yeah.

00:01:41.803 --> 00:01:43.469
- Yeah.
- It's such a cool instrument.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:44.500
It's so cool sounding too.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.150
- [Kelly] It's a sexy instrument.

